{
  "dom_id": "step-q14773",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$\\int 2{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{4}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}$ | ${e}^{4x}$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}}{2}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{{x}^{3}{e}^{4x}}{2}$ |\n| $48x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3{x}^{2}{e}^{4x}}{8}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{256}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{16}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{1024}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{64}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\int 2{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
      "choices": [
